#
# The AppImage entry point. Kept to the three things it actually has to do,
# because everything else about this application is already inside the
# executable: Qt, HDF5 and the fonts are linked statically, so there are no
# plugin directories to point at and no qt.conf to write.
#
# What does have to happen is the library path. tools/make-appimage.sh bundles
# the handful of libraries RHEL 8 ships only in versions older than the build
# machine's -- the xcb-util family, libSM/libICE, libxkbcommon -- and they live
# in usr/lib next to nothing else. (libxcb-cursor, which RHEL 8 does not ship
# outside EPEL at all, used to be the important one here; it is linked into the
# executable now. See ports/xcb-util-cursor.)
#
# POSIX sh rather than bash: this runs before anything is known about the host,
# and /bin/sh is the one interpreter that is always there.

APPDIR="$(dirname "$(readlink -f "$0")")"
export LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$APPDIR/usr/lib${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH}"

# The binary is named for its version, so the AppDir carries an unversioned
# symlink beside it and this never has to know which release it is in.
exec "$APPDIR/usr/bin/H5Scope" "$@"
